{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"promise-combinators","title":"Promise.all, allSettled, race & any","group":"Asynchronous JavaScript","order":44,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Four static methods run many promises concurrently and combine the results — they differ only in <em>when they settle</em> and <em>what counts as failure</em>.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Fulfils when</th><th>Rejects when</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Promise.all</code></td><td><strong>All</strong> fulfil</td><td><strong>Any</strong> rejects (fail-fast)</td><td>Array of values, in input order</td></tr><tr><td><code>Promise.allSettled</code></td><td>All settle</td><td>Never</td><td>Array of <code>{status, value \\| reason}</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Promise.race</code></td><td>The <strong>first to settle</strong> fulfils</td><td>The first to settle rejects</td><td>That one value/reason</td></tr><tr><td><code>Promise.any</code></td><td>The <strong>first to fulfil</strong></td><td><strong>All</strong> reject</td><td>Value, or <code>AggregateError</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const ok = (ms, v) =&gt; new Promise((res) =&gt; setTimeout(() =&gt; res(v), ms));\nconst bad = (ms, msg) =&gt; new Promise((_, rej) =&gt; setTimeout(() =&gt; rej(new Error(msg)), ms));\n\nconsole.log(\"all:\", await Promise.all([ok(30, \"a\"), ok(10, \"b\"), 42]));\nawait Promise.all([ok(10, \"a\"), bad(5, \"db down\")]).catch((e) =&gt; console.log(\"all rejected:\", e.message));\n\nconst settled = await Promise.allSettled([ok(5, \"a\"), bad(5, \"nope\")]);\nconsole.log(settled.map((r) =&gt; (r.status === \"fulfilled\" ? r : { ...r, reason: r.reason.message })));\n\nconsole.log(\"race:\", await Promise.race([ok(20, \"slow\"), ok(5, \"fast\")]));\nconsole.log(\"any:\", await Promise.any([bad(5, \"x\"), ok(15, \"first success\")]));\ntry {\n  await Promise.any([bad(5, \"e1\"), bad(5, \"e2\")]);\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.constructor.name, e.errors.map((x) =&gt; x.message));\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>all: [ 'a', 'b', 42 ]\nall rejected: db down\n[\n  { status: 'fulfilled', value: 'a' },\n  { status: 'rejected', reason: 'nope' }\n]\nrace: fast\nany: first success\nAggregateError [ 'e1', 'e2' ]</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p><code>Promise.all</code> rejects fast, but the other operations <strong>keep running</strong> — promises are not cancellable. Use an <code>AbortController</code> if you need to stop them.</p></div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-clock-x\"></i>Pattern: timeout with race</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const timeout = (ms) =&gt; new Promise((_, rej) =&gt; setTimeout(() =&gt; rej(new Error(`timed out after ${ms}ms`)), ms));\nconst slowFetch = new Promise((res) =&gt; setTimeout(() =&gt; res(\"data\"), 50));\ntry {\n  await Promise.race([slowFetch, timeout(10)]);\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.message);\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>timed out after 10ms</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-right\"></i>Sequential vs parallel</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const job = (id, log) =&gt; new Promise((res) =&gt; setTimeout(() =&gt; { log.push(id); res(id); }, 10 * (4 - id)));\n\nconst seq = [];\nfor (const id of [1, 2, 3]) await job(id, seq);          // one after another\nconsole.log(\"sequential finish order:\", seq);\n\nconst par = [];\nconst results = await Promise.all([1, 2, 3].map((id) =&gt; job(id, par)));  // all at once\nconsole.log(\"parallel finish order:\", par, \"results:\", results);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>sequential finish order: [ 1, 2, 3 ]\nparallel finish order: [ 3, 2, 1 ] results: [ 1, 2, 3 ]</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Promise.all vs Promise.allSettled?</summary><div><p><code>all</code> fails fast: it rejects with the first error and you lose the other results. <code>allSettled</code> always waits for every promise and reports each outcome, so use it when partial success is acceptable (e.g. sending many notifications).</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>race vs any?</summary><div><p><code>race</code> settles with the first promise to settle, success or failure. <code>any</code> ignores rejections and fulfils with the first success; it rejects only if all reject (with an <code>AggregateError</code>).</p></div></details></section>"}